    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 28th with a high-ceiling core, led by **Junior Caminero** (74.76) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.67), who represent our strongest plays of the day. **Junior Caminero** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Me, Kelly, whose 4.85 xERA provides the most exploitable surface of the slate, while **Yordan Alvarez** continues to operate in an elite tier, sporting a 0.444 xwOBA that remains impervious to Flaherty\u2019s rotation. **Trea Turner** (69.55) and **Kyle Schwarber** (68.77) are also cleared for significant volume; while both face a minor park penalty, their high-leverage order positions and favorable platoon dynamics against P\u00e9rez, C keep them firmly in the \"Strong\" start category. Notably, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.08) offers unique value today; despite a lower base projection, the combination of his top-tier sprint speed and a high-efficiency matchup against Woodruff makes him a priority for our critical SB accumulation goal.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (39.35), who fell just shy of our 40.0 floor. While **Carson Benge** brings consistent contact skills, his matchup against Luzardo\u2019s 3.33 xERA, compounded by a restrictive L/L platoon disadvantage, forced him to the bench in favor of higher-floor contributors. We are monitoring **Caleb Durbin** (57.10) closely, as his status remains pending; should he be scratched from the lineup, we may look toward the bench, though the drop-off in production from **Dillon Dingler** (37.30) and **Casey Schmitt** (36.09) suggests we should exercise caution with any mid-day swaps. Risk remains elevated for **Christian Yelich** (56.89), whose score was dragged down by a -13% dynamic platoon penalty against Rolison, and **Gary Sanchez** (55.65), who remains a marginal start as he contends with the same pitcher. Managers should be aware that **Hyeseong Kim** remains unavailable due to his current status with the Oklahoma City Comets.",
